      "rendered": false,
      "scraped": false,
      "excerpts": [
        "Procrastination is one of the most common and perplexing human behaviours.",
        "Almost everyone has experienced intending to do one thing but ending up doing something entirely different.",
        "Despite knowing that delaying important tasks leads to stress, reduced performance, and regret, people continue to procrastinate.",
        "Psychologists, neuroscientists, and behavioural economists have long tried to understand why humans act against their own long-term interests.",
        "Procrastination is not just laziness; it is a complex behavior rooted in biology, emotions, cognitive habits, and environmental influences.",
        "The tension between the emotional brain and the rational brain often drives procrastination.",
        "Tasks that feel overwhelming or boring activate the limbic system, which seeks immediate comfort and pushes us toward easier or more pleasurable activities.",
        "As a result, people gravitate toward distractions like social media instead of working on challenging tasks.",
        "This research paper aims to explore the psychological, emotional, and cognitive factors that contribute to procrastination and understand why this behavior continues despite its long-term negative outcomes."
      ]
