      "title": "Why We Procrastinate: A Psychological Perspective",
      "publisher": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF RESEARCH & SOCIAL SCIENCES",
      "author": "Muhammad Naseem Abid",
      "published_at": "2026-02-23",
      "url": "https://openalex.org/W7220226530",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-10-18T14:50:37.705Z",
      "sha256": "d9308269231d5eb1f2ab8ab9388054fda45ef27d001ab907fdec01dbc2b42ee2",
      "rendered": false,
      "scraped": false,
      "excerpts": [
        "Procrastination is a prevalent behavioral issue that significantly impairs personal and professional functioning.",
        "Despite its ubiquitous nature, procrastination remains a subject of widespread intrigue and debate within psychological research.",
        "This article examines procrastination through a psychological lens, exploring its underlying causes, cognitive processes, emotional influences, and potential consequences.",
        "By reviewing existing literature, the study seeks to provide a deeper understanding procrastination's multifaceted nature, from the role of self-regulation and impulsivity to the influence of fear and perfectionism.",
        "The paper also considers the impact of procrastination on mental health, performance, and decision making.",
        "Interventions and strategies for overcoming procrastination are discussed, focusing on cognitive-behavioral approaches, mindfulness, and time management techniques.",
        "The article concludes with suggestions for future research avenues to further explore the intricate dynamics of procrastination."
      ]
